			<div class="content" id="post-content-4462734">
									

<p>I want to like this, but there are a few things that led me to downvote.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Kiara looks to an infographic that is obscured by an instances of SCP-4728.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>an instances should be &quot;an instance&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Hey there Circuit Breakers today were going to talk about DVDs which is a new format and people are using it to store all of their real life movies on it, and animated movies as well.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sounds unnatural and could use some commas, such as after 'breakers' and 'DVDs'. Also, &quot;were going to talk&quot; should be &quot;we're going to talk.&quot;</p>
<p>There are some other miscellaneous grammar issues throughout the logs as well. I'd advise you read the logs back to yourself, out loud, and try to make it sound more natural, like adding pauses where pauses sound nice, all that. Except for the areas where it shouldn't sound natural, of course.</p>
<p>That being said, I'm not a huge fan of the whole &quot;Replace&quot; gimmick of linking back to the same article. I understand it, but&#8230; eh. Just not doing it for me. -1.</p>

